@startuml
title Create Game – Quickstart (1 human + 3 bots, auto-start)

actor "Player" as P
participant "Frontend\n(React + Zustand)" as FE
participant "REST API" as REST
participant "STOMP\n(WebSocket)" as STOMP
participant "GameService" as SVC
database "DB" as DB

== Create the game ==
P -> FE : select variant + bot difficulty, click "Create Game"\n(mode = singleplayer → quickStart)
FE -> REST : POST /api/games { variantId, botDifficulty }
REST -> SVC : createGame()
SVC -> DB : save game, contracts, creator seat
SVC --> REST : gameId
REST --> FE : 201 Created — { gameId }

== Connect to the game ==
FE -> STOMP : connect to /ws, subscribe to game channels\n(/app/…/lobby · /app/…/public-state · /app/…/private-state)
STOMP --> FE : lobby snapshot (creator seated, game not started)\npublic-state and private-state return null until game starts

== Game start (no Lobby screen, no manual click) ==
FE -> STOMP : on WebSocket connect, automatically\nSEND /app/games/{id}/lobby/start

STOMP -> SVC : fillWithBots(gameId)
SVC -> DB : save 3 bot player rows
SVC --> STOMP : LobbyEventDTO
STOMP --> FE : /topic/games/{id}/lobby — all 4 seats filled

STOMP -> SVC : startGame(gameId)
SVC -> DB : set status IN_PROGRESS; replay() → initialState
SVC --> STOMP : GameUpdateBundle (initial state)
STOMP --> FE : /topic/games/{id} — initial game state\n(first player must select a contract)
STOMP --> FE : /user/queue/games/{id}/private-state — player's hand
FE -> P : show Game Board

@enduml